## Why This Is Asked
This question tests understanding of streaming cardinality estimation under memory constraints—a fundamental skill for building analytics pipelines at scale.

## Key Concepts
- **HyperLogLog**: Uses probabilistic counting to estimate cardinalities with sub-linear memory
- **Register updates**: Hash to determine bucket, count leading zeros, store maximum run length
- **Merge behavior**: Element-wise maximum of registers enables lossless parallel merging
- **Error bounds**: Relative standard error ≈ 1.04/√m; memory scales as O(m)

## Code Example
```javascript
class HyperLogLog {
  constructor(m = 128) {
    this.m = m;
    this.registers = new Uint8Array(m);
  }

  _hash(id) {
    let h = xmur3(id.toString());
    return splitmix64(h());
  }

  add(id) {
    const hash = this._hash(id);
    const idx = hash & (this.m - 1);
    const remaining = hash >>> Math.log2(this.m);
    const leadingZeros = Math.clz32(remaining) - (32 - Math.log2(this.m) - 1);
    this.registers[idx] = Math.max(this.registers[idx], leadingZeros + 1);
  }

  estimate() {
    const alpha = 0.7213 / (1 + 1.079 / this.m);
    const sum = this.registers.reduce((acc, val) => acc + Math.pow(2, -val), 0);
    return alpha * this.m * this.m / sum;
  }

  merge(other) {
    for (let i = 0; i < this.m; i++) {
      this.registers[i] = Math.max(this.registers[i], other.registers[i]);
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Maintaining the number of distinct substrings under incremental appends tests knowledge of suffix automata, amortized analysis, and practical update strategies. It highlights how to avoid recomputation and reason about state growth.

## Key Concepts
- Suffix Automaton (SAM) for distinct substrings
- Online extensions and delta = len(cur) - len(link(cur))
- Amortized analysis over batches
- Space linear in string length

## Code Example
```javascript
class SAMNode {
  constructor() {
    this.next = {};
    this.link = -1;
    this.len = 0;
  }
}
class SuffixAutomaton {
  constructor() {
    this.st = [new SAMNode()];
    this.last = 0;
    this.size = 1;
  }
  extend(c){
    const st = this.st; const cur = this.size++;
    st.push(new SAMNode()); st[cur].len = st[this.last].len + 1;
    let p = this.last;
    while (p >= 0 && !(c in st[p].next)) { st[p].next[c] = cur; p = st[p].link; }
    if (p === -1) { st[cur].link = 0; }
    else {
      const q = st[p].next[c];
      if (st[p].len + 1 === st[q].len) {
        st[cur].link = q;
      } else {
        const clone = this.size++;
        st.push(Object.assign(new SAMNode(), st[q]));
        st[clone].len = st[p].len + 1;
        while (p >= 0 && st[p].next[c] === q) { st[p].next[c] = clone; p = st[p].link; }
        st[q].link = st[cur].link = clone;
      }
    }
    this.last = cur;
  }
}
```

